INT. DEEP-SPACE LISTENING POST - COMMAND CENTRE - NIGHT

A circular room of screens and cables. Banks of antennae data scroll in green. One chair empty. A kettle ticks on a hotplate.

LIEUTENANT TEMITOPE "TEMI" AJAYI-NORDQVIST, 30s, in a dark jumpsuit, stares at a waveform. Beside her, COMMANDER BARNABY HOLLINGSWORTH-OSEI, 50s, leans on a console with a mug.

At the back, a stranger in a plain grey coat stands with his hands folded. THE VISITOR, 40s, calm, unlit by any badge.

TEMI
It's repeating.

BARNABY
How many cycles?

TEMI
Seventeen.

BARNABY
Direction?

TEMI
Cygnus.

BARNABY
Cygnus is empty.

TEMI
Cygnus was empty.

The Visitor steps forward. Barnaby turns.

BARNABY
Who authorised you down here?

VISITOR
No one yet.

BARNABY
That's not an answer.

VISITOR
It will be soon.

TEMI
Commander, the signal's changing.

BARNABY
Changing how?

TEMI
It's addressing us.

BARNABY
(setting down the mug)
Show me.

She taps a key. Text crawls up the main screen: a string of digits, then a single word.

HELLO

Silence. The kettle clicks off. At the rear console, SPECIALIST ORLANDO PAPADAKIS-NWOSU, 20s, hunched over headphones, pulls one earcup off and stares.

ORLANDO
Sir, I heard it too.

BARNABY (CONT'D)
That is a prank.

VISITOR
It isn't.

BARNABY
And you are?

VISITOR
Call me Ishmael.

BARNABY
That's not your name.

VISITOR
No. But it's one I chose.

TEMI
(whisper)
Commander, it's responding to him.

On the screen, the word changes: ISHMAEL.

Barnaby backs away. Temi grips her console. The man who calls himself Ishmael smiles faintly.

ISHMAEL
Thank you for answering.

BARNABY
We didn't.

ISHMAEL
Someone did. Long ago. I'm merely the postman.

TEMI
Who sent you?

ISHMAEL
Everyone you ever sent a signal to.

BARNABY
What do they want?

ISHMAEL
To say thank you.

TEMI
For what?

ISHMAEL
For being lonely.

Barnaby sits heavily in the empty chair. Temi presses a hand to her mouth. On the screen, a new line scrolls, unhurried, in a language none of them has seen, which all of them somehow read.
